# LogManthan OT tuning for Suricata's bundled Modbus and DNP3 event rules (Suricata 8.0.7).
#   modbus-events.rules  SIDs 2250001-2250009
#   dnp3-events.rules    SIDs 2270000-2270007
#
# Policy: rate-limit, don't disable. Each event still alerts, but at most once per source per
# window, so a fuzzing or malformed-traffic source stays visible without thousands of alerts.
# Nothing here touches the LM-OT rules (9100001-9199999); the test suite enforces that.
#
# Measured on the ITI ModbusTCP/ModbusTCP.pcap (85 s, 6331 event alerts before tuning) and the
# repo's test captures; see `python3 scripts/test_suricata.py` (Tuning section) for before/after.
#
# TODO(rajeev): how this reaches LogManthan's Suricata. Either point suricata.yaml at it
#   (threshold-file: /path/to/tuning/threshold.config) or merge these lines into the existing
#   threshold.config. Confirm which, and whether LogManthan already has entries for these SIDs
#   (a second entry for the same SID would conflict).
#
# Format: threshold gen_id 1, sig_id <sid>, type limit, track by_src, count 1, seconds <window>
# Comments must be on their own line: Suricata rejects a line with a trailing comment
# (and still starts, silently ignoring it).

# ---------- Modbus (modbus-events.rules) ----------
# Malformed or out-of-spec traffic. Can mean fuzzing, a scanner or a broken device: keep visible.
# invalid Protocol version
threshold gen_id 1, sig_id 2250001, type limit, track by_src, count 1, seconds 300
# unsolicited response (1765 before on ITI ModbusTCP)
threshold gen_id 1, sig_id 2250002, type limit, track by_src, count 1, seconds 300
# invalid Length (1006 before)
threshold gen_id 1, sig_id 2250003, type limit, track by_src, count 1, seconds 300
# invalid Function code (fuzzing signal)
threshold gen_id 1, sig_id 2250005, type limit, track by_src, count 1, seconds 300
# invalid Value (524 before)
threshold gen_id 1, sig_id 2250006, type limit, track by_src, count 1, seconds 300
# Exception code invalid
threshold gen_id 1, sig_id 2250007, type limit, track by_src, count 1, seconds 300
# Request flood (parser backlog)
threshold gen_id 1, sig_id 2250009, type limit, track by_src, count 1, seconds 300

# Data mismatch: rate-limited harder (1 per source per hour), not disabled.
# Suricata 8.0.7 sets error_flags DATA_VALUE on every FC3/FC4 (read registers) response, even when
# the response is correct. Known bug in the sawp-modbus parser: CybercentreCanada/sawp issue #13
# (register reads checked with the coil formula ceil(quantity/8)). Verified on our own lab traffic: FC3 quantity 10 -> byte count 20 and
# 20 data bytes (spec-correct), yet all 1127 lab FC3 responses alert. Same on the bro/modbus capture
# (quantity 2 -> 4 data bytes). So on register reads this is pure noise from the parser.
# It is NOT disabled because it also fires on coil reads/writes (FC1/FC15 in ITI ModbusTCP), where
# it may be a real mismatch. One alert per source per hour keeps that signal.
# Fixed on sawp main (commit 7f33f7e) but not yet released: sawp-modbus 0.14.0 still has the bug,
# and Suricata 8.0.7 ships 0.13.1.
# TODO(rajeev): remove this 1-hour limit (back to 300 s like the others) once a Suricata release
#   ships a sawp-modbus that includes 7f33f7e.
# Data mismatch (3036 before)
threshold gen_id 1, sig_id 2250008, type limit, track by_src, count 1, seconds 3600

# ---------- DNP3 (dnp3-events.rules) ----------
# None of these fired on our captures; limited the same way so a broken or hostile source can't flood.
# 2270005 (too many points) and 2270006 (too many objects) are left alone: they already carry
# their own threshold (type backoff, track by_flow) inside the bundled rule.
# Request flood
threshold gen_id 1, sig_id 2270000, type limit, track by_src, count 1, seconds 300
# Length too small
threshold gen_id 1, sig_id 2270001, type limit, track by_src, count 1, seconds 300
# Bad link CRC
threshold gen_id 1, sig_id 2270002, type limit, track by_src, count 1, seconds 300
# Bad transport CRC
threshold gen_id 1, sig_id 2270003, type limit, track by_src, count 1, seconds 300
# Unknown object
threshold gen_id 1, sig_id 2270004, type limit, track by_src, count 1, seconds 300
# Too long reassembly
threshold gen_id 1, sig_id 2270007, type limit, track by_src, count 1, seconds 300
